## 📢 **Latest Updates**

- **🔁 Claude Code-inspired loop primitives (v2.92.2):** Audited Claude Code's agent loop against CVC's existing primitives (arxiv 2604.14228 + code.claude.com docs). Two P0 gaps closed: `CostBudget` — USD spend cap analog of `max_budget_usd` (thread-safe, refundable, swappable pricing function), and `ToolRiskRegistry` — 4-tier reversibility-weighted permission system (`read_only` / `reversible_write` / `network_write` / `destructive`) with `--accept-network` / `--yes-destroy` CLI flags. CVC now has iteration budget + cost budget + permission tiers — the three legs Claude Code stands on.
- **🧠 Skill Insights (v2.92.0 + v2.92.1):** The world's first *cognitive* skill analytics. CVC is the only agent runtime that knows which skills the model *sees* (view_count) vs *actually uses* (use_count). `cvc skills insights` shows hot / fading / dead / fresh buckets plus a `[RECOMMENDED ACTIONS]` section with copy-pasteable CLI commands. Add `--apply-archives` to one-shot archive every dead skill (skips pinned + bundled). Available in CLI, dashboard (`/api/skills/insights`), and JSON.
- **Google Cloud Vertex AI Support:** Added Vertex AI adapter for OpenAI-compatible REST endpoint with Google Cloud Application Default Credentials (ADC) authentication, plus model fetching and enhanced CLI support.
- **Cognitive Features F1-F10 Testing:** Comprehensive end-to-end tests implemented for all core cognitive features, including the Cognitive Commit Learning Extractor, Versioned User Identity Model, DAG Dreaming, Quantum Branch Tournament, and Predictive Context Preloader.
- **Version 2.2.1 Released:** Added comprehensive update notes for v2.2.1 covering significant architectural changes and the newest cognitive features.
- **OpenClaw Integration (Beta):** OpenClaw is now successfully installed on our **Mac Mini** host! We are currently working on a deep integration between **CVC** and **OpenClaw** to enable seamless cognitive versioning for all OpenClaw agents.
- **Enhanced Agent Tools:** v1.8.50 includes updated prompt instructions for the built-in agent to better handle high-volume token responses and complex JSON structures.

<br>

