### 🧠 **Skill Insights (new in v2.92.0)**

**The world's first cognitive skill analytics.** CVC is the only agent
runtime that tracks which skills the model *sees* in the system prompt
versus which ones it actually uses. The gap between those two numbers
is **wasted context budget** — every dead skill burns tokens on every
single turn, forever.

```bash
$ cvc skills insights
[CVC Skill Insights] 2026-06-21T17:36:35+00:00
----------------------------------------------------------------
95 skills | 95 active | 0 stale | 0 archived | 0 pinned
avg use/view: 0.253  wasted context share: 0.0%

[HOT (used 3+ in 7d)] 8 skill(s) — cvc-add-new-provider / ...
[FADING (was used, 30d+ idle)] (none)
[DEAD (viewed 3+ but never used — wastes context)] (none)

[RECOMMENDED ACTIONS]
  3 suggested action(s) — ~12100 tokens potentially saved per turn

  [ARCHIVE] totally-dead  (caution)
    shown to the model 30 times, never picked — wastes ~6600 tokens/turn
    > cvc skills archive totally-dead

  [UNPIN] pinned-and-dead  (safe)
    pinned but never used — curator can't manage it
    > cvc skills unpin pinned-and-dead
```

Add `--apply-archives` to actually archive every dead skill (skips
pinned + bundled). Dashboard renders the same data via
`GET /api/skills/insights`. JSON mode: `cvc skills insights --json`.

